                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm going to break this down into Pros and Cons sections:\n\nPROS:\n+ Simple and easy to play\n+ Appropriate for all age groups\n+ Low system requirements\n+ Doesn't require a time commitment\n\nCONS:\n- Simplistic to a fault\n- Relatively poor graphics\n- Similar games have been released for FREE on Flash game websites\n- Extremely annoying protagonist who constantly pops up to tell you inane things\n- Can't skip (the very long and boring) tutorial at the beginning of the game\n\nBottom Line: If you have very young children or need a time waster on an underpowered laptop, this might do the trick. Otherwise, skip it if you're looking for a management game, as this won't scratch that itch.\n\nI'm going to give a \"NO\" recommendation simply because the majority of gamers on Steam probably won't fit into either of those categories. If I could, I've post a neutral rating, as it really depends what you want out of the game, but unfortunately, Steam doesn't allow that.",
